CORE
main.cpp

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^.*found no match for symbol 'operator\(\)'.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
--
Regression for function-template overload resolution: the body of a
named template specialization must not be instantiated while forming a
call's candidate set.  Only the selected overload's body is instantiated
([temp.inst]/2, [over.match]).  This is the arith_tools `numeric_cast_v`
pattern, where the non-selected `numeric_cast_v(const mp_integer&)`
overload has a body that is ill-formed for Target=mp_integer; eagerly
instantiating it reported a spurious "found no match for symbol
'operator()'".
